          "id": "124_cohorts_are_rated_and_every_species_block_is_the_same_104",
          "description": "THE STRUCTURAL CLAIM OF THIS RUNG, and no row count can make it: 1,288 rows is equally consistent with 129 + 103 x 5. S10 selects 125 of the 164 candidates for five of the six pollutant-processes and NONE for 7901 -- `pollutantprocessmodelyear` carries no NMHC row, so an NMHC rate row is not a rate row at all, which costs nothing because a chained row's existence never consults `rt_isSelected`. 124 of the 125 are rated: model year 2000 electricity has no `emissionratebyage` ageGroup-2099 row for fuel type 9 and is dropped, while 2001-2020 electricity are rated at exactly zero. Each of the five species blocks is 104 -- the 124 minus every electricity cohort -- and they are the SAME 104, because all three stages fail on the same missing `methanethcratio` row for fuel subtype 90 and each inherits the failure from the one above. 644 rate rows emit, which is what `n_outputRateRow` declares.\n\nWHAT IS ASSERTED is a sample of rate rows, not the counts: a rated, surviving, emitting gasoline row (124), the selected-but-unrated MY 2000 electricity row (144), species rows that do not emit for want of a ratio (780, 944, 288), and a species row that does not survive on its own rate (165). The per-pollutant-process selected and emitted counts, the 644 total, and the per-depth emission flags are gone from the model, and `cohortSurvivorCount` now counts the cohorts the output carries (124, not 125); none of them is asserted here.",
